# tests/captures/classes_trie_bounded.rxt — [M4.5e] close-lane coverage fill.
#
# A targeted assessment against the base tier's construct list (docs/dev/
# plan.md [M4.5e]) found the existing corpus (basic.rxt + the three D27
# territory files) thin or absent in three places, and adequate everywhere
# else it was checked (caseless via -i: 2 cases already; anchors ^/$: covered
# by zw-03/zw-04/alt-priority-06/anchor-01; startpos: covered by basic.rxt's
# `ms` case plus five anchor-0X-startpos cases) — those are NOT repeated
# here.
#
#   CLASSES: every existing capture case that touches module `classes` uses
#   `\d` only (basic.rxt's `(\d+)-(\d+)`, structure_anchors_misc.rxt's
#   `classes-bounded`). No bracket expression `[...]` — base grammar, no
#   module needed — ever appears inside a capturing group anywhere in the
#   corpus, and neither does `\w`/`\s`.
#
#   TRIE-SHAPED ALTERNATIONS: the corpus's largest alternation under a
#   capturing group is 3-way (`(a)|(b)|(c)`, unset-06-three-way). The trie
#   prefix-factoring pass (M2.8, src/ir/nfa.c) is proved output-preserving
#   independently (tests/codegen/run_trie_identity.sh, 500 generated
#   patterns) and never touches the VM's own alt-chain emission (emit_vm.c's
#   vm_alt walks the SAME AST directly, no trie involved) — so what is
#   actually missing is confidence that the VM's alt-chain gets captures
#   right at a branch count and prefix-sharing shape beyond the smallest
#   cases, not a trie-specific correctness question.
#
#   BOUNDED REPEATS AT THE K19 CAP BOUNDARY: every bounded-repeat capture
#   case in priority_and_iteration.rxt (iter-19..iter-27) uses a body with NO
#   alternation, so none of them ever engages replication at all — a bounded
#   repeat over a single-path body compiles to the §2.5 span-loop cursor
#   regardless of its count (tests/vm/run_vm_tests.sh's `spanok` case).
#   PCREC_MAX_VM_REPEAT_COPIES=64 (docs/dev/known_issues.md K19) only
#   applies to a bounded repeat over a CHOICE-BEARING body, and no existing
#   capture case has one anywhere near that count (run_vm_tests.sh's own
#   bigbounded/smallbounded pair, {0,20}/{0,3}, is a codegen-size check, not
#   a captures.rxt case, and neither approaches 64).
#
# Every expectation below is oracle-verified against python3 `re` AND
# checked against the real build/pcrec VM output before landing (same
# double-check basic.rxt's own header describes). All slots here are LIVE
# (`g`, not `gp`): every pattern below is captures-default, so it compiles
# to the VM (RX_NCAPS > 1) on every build this corpus runs against — no
# DFA-only pending case applies post-[M4.5b].

# ---- classes: bracket expressions, never exercised inside a capture -------

# case: classes-b01-bracket-range
pattern ([a-z]+)
# a bracket range, not \d -- base grammar, no module needed
m "abc123" 0 3
g 0 0 3
g 1 0 3

# case: classes-b02-negated-bracket
pattern ([^0-9]+)
# negated bracket class
m "abc123" 0 3
g 1 0 3

# case: classes-b03-inline-class
pattern (a[bc]d)
# a small in-line class as one element of a literal run, sandwiched inside
# other text on both sides
m "xacdx" 1 4
g 1 1 4

# case: classes-b04-w-s-two-groups
pattern (\w+)\s(\w+)
features classes
# \w and \s together, two groups separated by the class that matches neither
m "hello world" 0 11
g 1 0 5
g 2 6 11

# case: classes-b05-caseless-bracket
pattern ([a-z]+)
flags i
# a bracket class made case-insensitive: covers the classes gap and the
# caseless tier together rather than as two separate near-duplicate cases
m "ABCxyz" 0 6
g 1 0 6

# ---- trie-shaped alternations: beyond the corpus's existing 3-way cap -----

# case: trie-01-shared-prefix-5way
pattern (cat|car|carpet|dog|do)
# 5-way alternation with TWO disjoint shared-prefix families ("ca-", "do-"),
# each family itself ordered shorter-before-longer -- exactly
# run_trie_identity.sh's rule-1 shape (a branch that ENDS at a shared prefix
# node competes with a longer branch continuing through it), now checked
# with the alternation inside a CAPTURING group instead of a bare match.
m "carpet" 0 3
g 1 0 3
m "cat" 0 3
g 1 0 3
m "dog" 0 3
g 1 0 3
m "dolly" 0 2
g 1 0 2

# case: trie-02-disjoint-4way
pattern (dog|cat|bird|fish)
# a 4-way alternation with no shared prefixes at all -- the companion shape
# to trie-01, at the same branch count tests/codegen/CLAUDE.md's own
# 4-branch trie-eligibility control uses, captured instead of bare
m "fish" 0 4
g 1 0 4

# ---- bounded repeats at the K19 replication-cap boundary -------------------

# case: bounded-k19-01-at-cap
pattern ((a)|b){0,64}c
# a CHOICE-BEARING body ((a)|b) at exactly 64 repetitions -- the largest
# count PCREC_MAX_VM_REPEAT_COPIES allows before D45/K19's pre-emission
# refusal fires (checked separately, at 65, by tests/vm/run_vm_tests.sh's
# PCREC_MAX_VM_REPEAT_COPIES case, which asserts only that the artifact
# compiles -- this case asserts what it COMPUTES). 20 real iterations of
# alternating a/b, one char consumed per copy: the LAST iteration (index 19,
# 'b') writes only group 1 (the outer group wraps both branches); the
# iteration before it (index 18, 'a') was the last one to take the 'a'
# branch and write group 2, and that value persists through the final 'b'
# iteration, which never touches it -- ordinary "unwritten slots retain
# their last value" behaviour (S3.2), now checked at the replication cap.
m "ababababababababababc" 0 21
g 1 19 20
g 2 18 19
